            <ArticleTitle>Adrenal infarction in a healthy pregnant woman.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>90-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1753495X15627959</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adrenal infarction is a very rare event but occasionally seen in hypercoagulable states. We present a case of a 31-year-old woman at 38 weeks of gestation who developed a severe upper abdominal pain and unilateral adrenal infarction due to thrombosis of the adrenal vein. The only thrombogenic factor found was pregnancy. The case highlights that adrenal infarction may complicate a normal pregnancy and should be included in the differential diagnosis of the acute abdomen in pregnancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
